  "details": "- CVE-2026-123867: apply the CA of a TLS SNI context that was added without a\n  certificate, so client certificates for that host are verified against the\n  context's own CA instead of the default context's CA\n- CVE-2026-123868: charge inbound HTTP/2 DATA that paused streams still hold\n  against maxSessionMemory and stop reading from the socket once the budget\n  is spent, so a peer can no longer make a session retain unbounded memory\n  with many tiny DATA frames\n- CVE-2026-123872: bind TLS session resumption to the SNI server name, keep\n  the server name of the first ClientHello for renegotiation and\n  HelloRetryRequest, and disable resumption on mTLS servers that have no\n  session id context",
